~ start
- Meet at an ice cream shop
	Leona and Coral meet at Seabreeze Sundaes 
	Leona: Hello Darlin’. You must be Coral, nice to meet you.
	Coral: Yes, that’s me! Thank you for meeting me today. Have you decided on a flavor for your sundae? My little one, Marlin, loves sea salt. 
	Leona: I like that one, too. Marlin knows what he’s talkin’ about! But honey, what’s your favorite? I’m not datin’ Marlin now.
	Coral: I don’t really know, to be honest. I usually just finish whatever Marlin can’t. Guess mine would be sea salt, too.
	Leona: Oh sweetheart, you have to live for yourself sometimes, too. It’s obvious you care deeply for Marlin, but don’t lose yourself in the process. 
	Coral: You’re right, my whole life revolves around Marlin. I've forgotten how to live for myself sometimes.
	Leona: Let’s get samples of every flavor. We will find your favorite flavor today darlin’. 
	Leona charms the ice cream scooper to allow herself and Coral to taste every flavor at Seabreeze Sundaes.
	Coral: Beach day is definitely the best, the graham cracker sand is the perfect topping. Thank you for reminding myself to live my own life.
	Leona: That’s what I do best. I’m actually choosing myself from here on out, too. I want to enjoy the breeze in my hair freely, and eat at Seabreeze Sundaes whenever I want. Thank you for reminding me how fun it can be to choose yourself. 
	After date
	Coral: Leona reminded me not to lose myself while raising Marlin and it was such an important lesson. Of course Marlin will always be a great part of my world, but not my whole world. 
	+0 satisfaction. Neither heartbroken, neither fulfilled 
	Leona: Coral is such a sweetheart and is invitin’ me out for ice cream again with Marlin. Being single is nice, but having a community is still important, you know. Just cause I’m choosin’ myself doesn’t mean I can’t be makin’ friends, darlin’!
	+5 satisfaction. Fulfilled  
